  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energy Transition Sector Development Program, Subprogram 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on ADB&#x2019;s assistance to Cambodia on climate change since 2011 and clean energy since 2016, the program will provide comprehensive support to the government&#x2019;s energy transformation agenda, to (i) mainstream renewable energy and energy efficiency while transitioning away from fossil fuels, (ii) adopt data-driven regulation and planning for the power system to enhance flexibility and resilience, and (iii) anchor infrastructure investments on planning with new technologies and business models as well as implementation through competitive procurement. The programmatic approach will enable sequenced actions to successively strengthen sector governance and the enabling environment, and to provide flexibility for learning and updates, in phases, in the dynamic context of recovery from the coronavirus disease (COVID19) pandemic. The program&#x2019;s combination of policy reforms and project investments will mutually reinforce each other and maximize ADB&#x2019;s value addition. The policy actions enable and provide a platform for public and private sector investments in critical new technologies, such as energy efficiency and storage; set clean energy targets for the country; and integrate improved power development and energy use planning across sectors, including climate proofing critical infrastructure. The project investments will demonstrate new technologies in energy efficiency and storage including (i) the country&#x2019;s first grid-connected energy storage system, which will enable additional renewable sources to enter the grid and improve grid stability for consumers; and (ii) comprehensive city-level efficient street-lighting systems in Kampot and Kep provinces, which will demonstrate cost savings and benefits for tourism and public safety. The project component will also improve capacities for new technology scale-up to kick-start new markets.</narrative>
  </description>
